---
import ArticleLayout from "../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site";
import exCover from "../assets/ex-cover-kuchnia.png";
import exPhoto1 from "../assets/ex-kuchnia-photo1.png";
import psyChapter from "../assets/page-chapter.png";

const title = "AI Lead Magnet Generator — real ebooks";
const description =
  "Generate a researched, typeset ebook lead magnet in about an hour. AI research, writing, photographs, cover design, PDF + EPUB. One price from $9.99, no subscription.";

const faq = [
  {
    q: "Why an ebook instead of a checklist or template?",
    a: "Both have their place, and short formats convert well for quick wins. Ebooks carry the authority: in NetLine's analysis of 6.2 million B2B content registrations, ebooks took 39.5% of all demand — about four times more than guides and nearly six times more than white papers. When the goal is to be perceived as the expert, length and depth do the work.",
  },
  {
    q: "How long does it take to generate a lead magnet ebook?",
    a: "Structure appears within minutes for your approval; a complete book — written, illustrated, typeset, with a designed cover — typically lands in under an hour.",
  },
  {
    q: "Do I own the ebook and can I gate it behind an email form?",
    a: "Yes. Full commercial rights come with every book: gate it, sell it, print it, put your name on the cover. You receive a downloadable PDF and EPUB with no watermarks.",
  },
  {
    q: "What does it cost compared to hiring this out?",
    a: "A ghostwritten 5,000–10,000-word piece runs $1,000–10,000 at Reedsy marketplace rates, before design. An InkMagnet book costs $9.99–19.99 depending on length, including research, writing, images, cover and both formats.",
  },
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({
      "@type": "Question",
      name: f.q,
      acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: f.a },
    })),
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Service",
    name: "AI Lead Magnet Generator",
    provider: { "@type": "Organization", name: "InkMagnet", url: siteConfig.url },
    description,
    offers: {
      "@type": "AggregateOffer",
      priceCurrency: "USD",
      lowPrice: "9.99",
      highPrice: "19.99",
    },
  },
];
---

<ArticleLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  heading="The lead magnet generator that writes the book, not just the layout"
  subheading="Most 'lead magnet creators' hand you templates and wish you luck with the writing. InkMagnet researches your topic, writes every chapter, photographs it, designs the cover and typesets a book your subscribers will actually respect."
  crumbs={[
    { name: "InkMagnet", href: "/" },
    { name: "Lead magnet generator", href: "/lead-magnet-generator/" },
  ]}
  translated={true}
  hreflangEnPath="/lead-magnet-generator/"
  hreflangPlPath="/pl/generator-ebookow/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <h2>Why ebook lead magnets still earn their keep</h2>
  <p>
    The data on this is less ambiguous than the hot takes. In
    <a href="https://img.netline.com/images/netline/assets/2024-StateofB2B-ContentConsumption-DemandReport-NetLine.pdf" rel="nofollow">NetLine's analysis of 6.2 million real B2B content registrations</a>,
    ebooks captured 39.5% of all gated-content demand — the next format, guides,
    took 9.7%. On the conversion side,
    <a href="https://www.optimonk.com/popup-statistics" rel="nofollow">OptiMonk's popup statistics</a>
    show email popups offering an ebook converting at 7.49% against 5.10% for
    popups offering nothing, a 47% lift from the incentive alone. And the list
    you build with it pays back at
    <a href="https://www.litmus.com/resources/email-marketing-roi" rel="nofollow">$36 per $1 spent on email</a>,
    per Litmus.
  </p>
  <p>
    The honest caveat: an ebook only produces that effect when it looks worth
    gating. A reader who exchanges an email address for ten padded pages in a
    Canva template learns one thing about your brand, and it is not the thing
    you wanted. This is why the production bar matters more for lead magnets
    than almost any other content: the asset's entire job is to make you look
    like the expert.
  </p>

  <h2>What "generated" means here</h2>
  <p>
    InkMagnet is not a template editor with an AI button. The pipeline runs the
    way a small publishing team would:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Research.</strong> The engine searches the live web for your
      topic, scrapes the strongest sources and grounds the book in current
      material instead of model memory.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Structure you approve.</strong> A chapter-by-chapter outline
      arrives in minutes. You edit it or approve as is — nothing is written
      until you do.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Writing and review.</strong> Chapters are written with a
      consistent voice, then a separate review pass scores the draft and fixes
      weak sections before you ever see them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Pictures, cover, typesetting.</strong> Photographs are generated
      for specific passages, a cover is designed for this one book and
      reviewed for craft, and the whole thing is typeset by the engine
      academic publishers use — real hyphenation, running heads, drop caps.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The deliverable is a print-quality PDF and a store-ready EPUB, downloadable,
    watermark-free, with full commercial rights.
  </p>

  <figure>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3">
      <Image src={exCover} alt="AI-designed cover of a generated cookbook" width={400} />
      <Image src={exPhoto1} alt="Generated book page with AI food photography" width={400} />
      <Image src={psyChapter} alt="Chapter opening with drop cap from a generated book" width={400} />
    </div>
    <figcaption>
      Unretouched pages from customer books — <a href="/examples/">more in the examples gallery</a>,
      including a complete 38-page sample PDF.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>

  <h2>The math against doing it the old way</h2>
  <p>
    Producing a credible lead magnet ebook traditionally stacks three costs:
    writing, design and time.
    <a href="https://reedsy.com/blog/cost-to-hire-a-ghostwriter/" rel="nofollow">Reedsy's marketplace data</a>
    puts ghostwriting at $1,000–10,000 for the 5,000–10,000 words a typical
    lead magnet runs, book designers bill around $30–45 per hour on Upwork,
    and the calendar cost lands in weeks. InkMagnet compresses that into one
    run priced between $9.99 and $19.99, which changes what is rational: a
    lead magnet per campaign, per segment, per webinar — instead of one PDF
    serving the whole funnel for a year.
  </p>

  <h2>Where we draw the line</h2>
  <p>
    InkMagnet does not host opt-in forms or capture emails — tools like
    Beacon and OptinMonster do that well, and your email platform already has
    landing pages. We make the asset those forms give away. If you are
    comparing tools in this space, we keep honest, sourced comparisons of
    <a href="/vs/beacon-by/">InkMagnet vs Beacon</a>,
    <a href="/vs/designrr/">vs Designrr</a> and
    <a href="/vs/sqribble/">vs Sqribble</a> — including the points where they
    beat us.
  </p>

  <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
  {faq.map((f) => (
    <>
      <h3>{f.q}</h3>
      <p>{f.a}</p>
    </>
  ))}
</ArticleLayout>
